From: AX6 NSS Repair Project
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2026 11:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hwspinlock: qcom: bound MMIO regmap to resource size

The qcom,tcsr-mutex regmap advertises max_register 0x20000.  On
IPQ8074 the MMIO resource is also 0x20000 bytes, whose last complete
32-bit register starts at offset 0x1fffc.  Because max_register is
inclusive, a regmap debugfs dump reaches offset 0x20000 and accesses
one register beyond the mapping.

An IPQ8074 system reproduced the resulting fatal data abort in
regmap_mmio_read32le while userspace read the regmap debugfs file.  The
faulting register offset was 0x20000 and the process was grep.

Make a probe-local copy of the selected per-SoC regmap configuration
and clamp its upper bound to the last complete register in the MMIO
resource.  Preserve a smaller driver-defined upper bound when the DT
resource is larger, and reject resources smaller than one register to
avoid unsigned underflow.

Signed-off-by: AX6 NSS Repair Project
---
 drivers/hwspinlock/qcom_hwspinlock.c | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/hwspinlock/qcom_hwspinlock.c
+++ b/drivers/hwspinlock/qcom_hwspinlock.c
@@ -182,19 +182,36 @@ static struct regmap *qcom_hwspinlock_probe_mmio(struct platform_device *pdev,
 						 u32 *offset, u32 *stride)
 {
 	const struct qcom_hwspinlock_of_data *data;
+	struct regmap_config regmap_config;
 	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct resource *res;
+	resource_size_t size;
 	void __iomem *base;
 
 	data = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	if (!data->regmap_config)
 		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
 
 	*offset = data->offset;
 	*stride = data->stride;
 
+	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 0);
+	if (!res)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
+
+	size = resource_size(res);
+	if (size < data->regmap_config->reg_stride)
+		return ERR_PTR(-EINVAL);
+
 	base = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(base))
 		return ERR_CAST(base);
 
-	return devm_regmap_init_mmio(dev, base, data->regmap_config);
+
+	regmap_config = *data->regmap_config;
+	regmap_config.max_register = min_t(resource_size_t,
+					regmap_config.max_register,
+					size - regmap_config.reg_stride);
+
+	return devm_regmap_init_mmio(dev, base, &regmap_config);
 }
